> factor x^6 - 1
factor x^6 - 1
  = (x - 1)*(x + 1)*(x^2 + x + 1)*(x^2 - x + 1)
  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)
  (factors are irreducible over the rationals)
> expand (x - 1)*(x + 1)*(x^2 + x + 1)*(x^2 - x + 1)
  ucas: expand (x - 1)*(x + 1)*(x^2 + x + 1)*(x^2 - x + 1)
expand (x - 1)*(x + 1)*(x^2 + x + 1)*(x^2 - x + 1)
  = x^6 - 1
  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)
> factor x^4 - 1
factor x^4 - 1
  = (x - 1)*(x + 1)*(x^2 + 1)
  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)
  (factors are irreducible over the rationals)
> expand (x - 1)*(x + 1)*(x^2 + 1)
  ucas: expand (x - 1)*(x + 1)*(x^2 + 1)
expand (x - 1)*(x + 1)*(x^2 + 1)
  = x^4 - 1
  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)
> factor x^3 - 3x^2 + 3x - 1
factor x^3 - 3x^2 + 3x - 1
  = (x - 1)^3
  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)
  (factors are irreducible over the rationals)
> expand (x - 1)^3
  ucas: expand (x - 1)^3
expand (x - 1)^3
  = x^3 - 3x^2 + 3x - 1
  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)
> factor x^8 - 1
factor x^8 - 1
  = (x - 1)*(x + 1)*(x^2 + 1)*(x^4 + 1)
  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)
  (factors are irreducible over the rationals)
> factor (x^2 + 1)*(x^2 + 2)
factor (x^2 + 1)*(x^2 + 2)
  = (x^2 + 1)*(x^2 + 2)
  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)
  (factors are irreducible over the rationals)
> expand (x^2 + 1)*(x^2 + 2)
  ucas: expand (x^2 + 1)*(x^2 + 2)
expand (x^2 + 1)*(x^2 + 2)
  = x^4 + 3x^2 + 2
  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)
